;; Problem statements, one per stage of the run, written before the stage is built (docs/hickey.md,
;; "And the hammock."): the problem, the information it needs that the bot does not yet gather, what
;; can go wrong, what done means in world terms, and what the last recorded failure showed. Hand-written
;; data next to goals.edn; problems_test requires a statement for every target goal and checks every
;; source exists. Stages already built cite our own recorded failures; stages ahead cite the siblings
;; (steve, ruststeve), whose notes in brain/siblings are research drafts until re-verified.
;; Update a row when a run of that stage fails in a new way: the failure is the most valuable line here.
[{:problem/stage :wood
  :problem/goals [:wood]
  :problem/statement
  "Hold one log from a natural tree, starting wherever the bot lands, with only what the server has sent it."
  :problem/needs
  ["Which loaded blocks are logs, and which log of a trunk is at feet height."
   "Where its own drop is, and whether a leaf covers it."
   "Whether the landing itself is usable: not water, not inside a canopy, not buried."]
  :problem/risks
  ["A drop lands under the trunk, out of a 1.8-tall player's reach."
   "A branch passes for a trunk bottom, or the trunk stands on a bank above the bot: the drop rests out of the pickup box."
   "A leaf at head height hides the drop and walking cannot pass it."
   "The fixture lands the bot on a pond, in a canopy or in stone."
   "An early FINISH aborts the break."]
  :problem/done "The server's inventory read for the bot shows any *_log."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Recorded in CI and replayed: collect failed :not-picked-up when the bot dug the base log from two blocks above (fixed by trunk-target), and again when a low oak leaf covered the drop (fixed by digging the blocker). Recorded live 2026-10-10 on a pickaxe run and diagnosed by folding the recording: three collects in a row failed :not-picked-up because the drop lay one block up a ledge with leaves one above head height over the ledge and over the bot, so no jump rose a full block (fixed: over a one-block step, the blocker also looks one above the head, in both columns). Recorded by the gym (batch wood-a2 run 5) and again by a plan (smoke2 run 5), landing 21280,18720, and diagnosed by folding the recording: the bot took a branch log (air under it) for a trunk bottom and its drop came to rest on the trunk below; then, standing in a pit, it dug the real base on a bank four blocks above its feet and that drop rested above its pickup box; each failed walk blacklisted one log, not the tree, so it kept choosing the same trunk until the plan failed :stuck. Fixed: a trunk bottom stands on ground (or over its own dug base), a log walk arrives only with the drop's resting height within pickup reach of the feet, and a failed log intent blacklists its whole trunk (sim scenarios a-drop-out-of-reach-is-never-dug-for and a-trunk-on-a-bank-is-taken-from-the-bank). The forest property now generates branches and banks 1-2 high; a tree on a 2-high bank holds its drop beyond a pickup from the ground, and the bot gives it up (:no-log when it is the only tree). Open: cut a step into a bank to stand level with its trunk. The walk now follows a planned route (issue #4): a pond or a two-block ledge between the bot and the trunk, which ended :stuck and blacklisted the trunk, is routed around or climbed by its step (sim scenario a-log-across-a-cliff-and-a-pond-is-reached-by-a-route). Race 38477665442 (issue #38, 39 bots, and the sim race in the same worlds): every bot landed on snowy ground never moved, twelve walks failing :no-path in a second, because one layer of snow lay on every block round it and a route took that layer for an awkward shape, so neither the feet cell nor any beside it could be stood on and every plan was :none from nowhere. Fixed: one layer of snow has no collision shape in the game and the physics passes through it, so a route does too (path/one-layer-snow; path-test a-snowfield-is-crossed-through-its-one-layer-snow)."
  :problem/sources
  ["brain/bot/gotchas/drop-under-the-trunk.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/leaf-canopy-over-the-drop.md"
   "brain/bot/tooling/harness-landing.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/early-finish-aborts.md"]}
