 {:problem/stage :stone-tools
  :problem/issue 9
  :problem/goals [:cobblestone]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot can only dig a log by hand on a constant 3000 ms timer, so it cannot know how long stone takes, which tool to hold, that stone dug by hand drops nothing, or how to get down to stone without falling into a cave, lake or lava."
  :problem/needs
  ["Real block hardness per block, read from the game's own classes at datagen (the --reports output has none)"
   "Harvest rules: the jar's mineable/* and needs_*_tool tags (which tool kind, which tier)"
   "Which inventory slot holds the best tool, and the server-confirmed held slot"
   "Whether the eyes are in water and whether the bot is on the ground (each a /5 dig penalty)"
   "Liquid and air-column contents of every cell a stair-down step would open"
   "Remembered stone positions to walk to (memory watches logs only today)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Dig time too short: client predicts air, server restores the block with a block-update"
   "Held slot drifts from the server's, so the bot digs with the wrong item and the break is rejected"
   "Stone dug by hand or iron ore with a wooden pickaxe takes 7.5 s and drops nothing"
   "Tool breaks mid-run and later digs fall back to bare hand"
   "Digging under the feet drops the bot into lava, water or a deep shaft"
   "Reporting a dig-down as success when the bot never actually fell, so the caller spins"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON Inventory shows at least 3 cobblestone with the wooden pickaxe still held, RESULT :ok true, and the recorded run replays to the same RESULT; crafting the stone pickaxe itself is left to the crafting issue."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Built 2026-10-10 (issue #9) against the model first: hardness, harvest tags and tool materials read from the game itself (stone has no tier, so a hand harvests it in 2300 ms, which the issue had wrong; a penalty divides the speed before ceil, 5650 ms not 5750); the dig chooses the fastest tool of the block's kind and refuses a tiered block no tool reaches; a refused break (the block restored after FINISH) fails :rejected; stairs down refuse water, lava and drops and never dig the support. The needs planner gained :goal/holds (a tool is required once, not per run) after it crafted three pickaxes for three cobblestone. Gym batch cobble-a1 (12 runs, set A): eleven timed out, the server logging 'lost connection: Timed out', because memory watched stone and held 120,000 sightings after ten chunks, so every chunk load and planner tick took seconds (fixed: exposed stone is the terrain's question, read from the loaded columns); the twelfth failed :no-path because six chunk arrivals each re-planned a found route (fixed: only a waypoint ahead gone unstandable re-plans). Batch cobble-a2: 10/12 pass, 44-93 s. Run 2 met iron ore four stairs down and the stair failed with the child's :needs-tool three times in a second (fixed: an undroppable cell turns the stair, like lava). Open, run 9 (landing 20480,19200): standing at y 73 on a hillside, the nearest exposed stone was at y 64 at the foot of a nine-block face; a cell beside it is standable, so it was chosen, but no route reaches it, and three such choices failed :no-path in a second. A stone target should be chosen only when a route reaches a cell beside it (plan before choosing), or stairs cut down instead. Found 2026-10-11 against the model (three-cobblestone): every stone collect waited out its 10 s and failed :not-picked-up, so three cobblestone took 63 s. The collect counted only logs; the walk ended on the surface two blocks above the stone, so the drop lay under the pickup box; and each failure blacklisted its stone, which hid that the stone search read the chunks without the overlay of the bot's own breaks (a dug stone was chosen again). Fixed: a collect counts its :intent/drops, a walk to stone ends where the stone is at the feet's height or up to two above them (path's :pickup goal; gym batch push70 showed one exact cell beside the stone can be walled off while a cell below it is reachable), and the search asks the overlay. Three cobblestone in the model now take about 11 s with no failed intent. ruststeve: placeholder hardness 1.0 made natural deepslate digs fail about half the time (the 1.35x+200 ms hold landed on the server's 70% threshold), and once both iron pickaxes wore out after ~550 digs, bare-hand descent ran ~44 s per block. Race 38477665442 (issue #42, 27 real bots and 674 sim runs a round): every bot landed in snow (runners 2, 6 and 10) cut its first stair into a snow block, which drops only to a shovel, and the staircase stopped :no-shovel for a tool it does not need, three times in a second. The stairs now stop only for a missing pickaxe; anything else is dug by hand. Same race, landing 2361,111,2361 (issue #65): a walk to stone stepped off a cliff, the dig failed :out-of-reach on the way down, and the staircase the mine started next was planned from the air, every heading refused for the drop, :boxed three times in the four seconds of the fall. A staircase now waits for the ground before it plans a stair. Same race, runner 9 (issue #59, and #66 at the ingots): with 25 bots on one server the acks of FINISH came 200-300 ms late and the breaks later or never (an early FINISH queued behind another and dropped), the dig ended on the ack alone with the cell overlaid as air, and the staircase walked into rock the server still had, put back by it ten times a second until the step timed out, :stair-not-taken three times. A dig now ends on the server's block update; its ack with the block still standing is :rejected, and the stairs dig that cell again."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/05-dig-with-tools-stone-pickaxe.md"
                    "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md" "brain/siblings/sib-dig-hardness.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dig-stop-timing.md" "brain/siblings/sib-held-slot-drift.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dig-down-safety.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :water-and-lava
  :problem/issue 5
  :problem/goals [:escape-water :escape-lava :shore]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot cannot tell it is in water or lava: liquids are passable air to the physics, nothing tracks breath, health or death, and the planner cannot interrupt a running intent, so a bot that walks into a pond sinks, walks the bottom and drowns without noticing."
  :problem/needs
  ["In-water, in-lava and eye-in-water flags written by the physics step every tick (eye at y+1.62, not feet+1)"
   "Fluid kind and level per block, from the block state ids"
   "Estimated air, fall distance, health-zero death and the respawn packet"
   "A bank to swim to: nearest column with air at eye height and solid support"
   "Water and lava sightings in memory, plus water-trap facts left behind after an escape"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Jump in water gives almost no lift; only pressing into a bank fires the 0.3 wall impulse"
   "Swimming in an arbitrary heading goes deeper and drowns"
   "Head goes under mid-intent and the bot drowns inside the step"
   "A one-tick bob to dry Y reads as escaped, then the next step shoves it back in"
   "Roofed aquifer: every move goes up into stone while air is sideways and down"
   "Standing beside or over lava; a lily pad lid stops the rise"]
  :problem/done
  "From a shore landing the bot walks into water and back out: RESULT reports :escaped true, RCON confirms no water at the feet or head cell and OnGround 1b, with at least 9 of 10 CI trials passing and zero deaths."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never attempted this. steve: the bot dove into cave water found 23 blocks down and was hard water-trapped in a 1-wide flooded pocket, losing the run (race81/192). ruststeve: rust-race-003 drowned in a water column under solid stone, every escape move going up while air was one block west and one down."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/06-water-and-lava-survival.md" "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
