 {:problem/stage :iron-kit
  :problem/issue 6
  :problem/goals [:furnace :ingots :bucket :water-bucket :flint-and-steel :iron-kit]
  :problem/statement
  "Between the stone pickaxe and the portal the bot must turn ore into ingots, buckets, a filled water bucket and flint and steel, and both siblings stalled here because fuel was never planned, furnace-window items went uncounted, and scoopable water was not found."
  :problem/needs
  ["Furnace window state: slots, state id, carried item, fuel and cook progress properties"
   "Fuel as a planned need: burn values per item summed over the inventory"
   "Sightings of coal ore, iron ore, gravel and surface water sources (air above, near the column surface)"
   "Iron already invested in buckets and flint and steel, so it is not re-mined"
   "Proof of a scoop: water_bucket appearing in the inventory"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Planks burned as fuel run dry after about 3 ingots and starve the wood chain"
   "Items in the furnace or grid are invisible to the inventory count, so steps flicker"
   "Closing the window with a loaded cursor drops the item on the ground"
   "No reachable surface water in a dry biome; the bot hangs at fill-water"
   "Cave or aquifer water is chosen and the bot drowns at the scoop"
   "Scoop echo lags, so an empty bucket is reported though the source was there"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON Inventory shows a filled water_bucket and flint_and_steel after a live run on the local server, with RESULT :ok true."
  :problem/last-failure
  "First live run (local server, forest landing 2360,2360, 2026-10-11): no iron in sight at the surface, so the bot cut stairs down toward y 16; at y 36 an aquifer lay beside the next stair's cells, the child dig refused :unsafe, and the staircase failed instead of turning, three times, ending the plan. The stairs now turn on it. Second run, same landing: past the aquifer to y 16, then the only iron in sight was at y 7 with no path to it, and at the row's depth of 16 the bot waited :none-in-sight until the plan failed; iron's depth is now 0. Third run: three iron mined, the furnace crafted and placed, three ingots smelted in 30 s, the bucket crafted, then three scoops at aquifer sources with stone over them, all acked and none filling the bucket; a scoop target now needs air above and a clear line of sight. Fourth run, same landing: three walks to iron in an old excavation below, each :no-path, ended the plan; targets are now chosen only where a route reaches. Fifth run, fresh landing 3024,2360: over an underground lake at y 52 every stair was refused and the staircase failed :boxed; it now takes a level step around. Sixth run, same landing: a new stone pickaxe crafted down the mine, then no iron in sight at y 0 and the plan failed :none-in-sight; at a row's depth it now tunnels outward. Seventh run, fresh landing 2360,3000: flint already held from gravel dug on the way, the staircase cut through gravel at y 37-40, and the gravel over the stair fell into the cells it opened: :stair-not-taken, then two digs whose cell had emptied, :target-gone; a refilled cell is now dug again and an emptied one counts as open. Gym batch iron-a2 (forest set A, afaea33): 0 of 5; every run mined, smelted and crafted the bucket underground, then runs 1, 2 and 5 waited :no-water at y 16-24 with no route back to the landing (an ore mined out of a stair's floor, a niche dug under one), run 3 walked out to a pond and failed :no-scoop although the server filled its bucket three times (a worn pickaxe's damage component cut short the inventory the server answered with, before the water bucket), and run 4 timed out; the bot now cuts stairs up when no route leads out and reads a worn tool's slot. Eighth run (local landing 2360,3000, 53744be): through the gravel to y 16, then its tunnels, refused east, turned and ran back west beside the first until the trial timed out. Ninth run (local landing 2360,2360, 8f7b2ae): iron mined at y 35 and 22, ingots smelted, the bucket crafted, then stairs cut up from y 22 to y 51, where water lay over every stair up and the level steps went round a square of four cells until :boxed; they now keep their way. Gym batch iron-a3 (8f7b2ae): 0 of 5, but run 3 filled its water bucket at a pond, the first real scoop seen; runs 1 and 3 then stopped :no-pickaxe holding a stone pickaxe in the main inventory, run 2 had broken its pickaxe and nothing made another for the climb out, run 5 failed its furnace :needs-tool on a niche of ore, run 4's tunnel was :boxed; tools are now put in hand from the main inventory, the bucket and gravel rows hold a pickaxe, and a niche is never a block the tools cannot drop. Tenth run (local landing 2360,2360, 237b892): the pickaxe broke on the climb, a new one was made, the stairs walked out from under the water and came up to y 60, into a pit two below a pond's surface with the water in reach and out of sight, and waited :no-water; a scoop walk now ends on the bank. Eleventh run (098ea42): the stairs up stopped under the open sky at y 60, two below the ground in a shaft one wide with no route out, and waited :no-water; the climb now ends only with a level way on under the sky. Gym batch iron-a4 (237b892): 0 of 5; run 3 held a filled water bucket and went down again for the fourth ingot, where its tunnels and run 4's were :boxed by aquifers three times in a second; a new tunnel now takes a heading it can cut, else goes deeper, and the kit plans the flint and steel first, so all four ingots and the flint are got in one trip down. Runs 2 and 5 waited :no-water after climbing out (the pit and shaft fixed since); run 1's climb took level steps under a riverbed, the gravel over a cut fell and the river came down the tunnel; a cell under gravel or sand with water or lava on it is now never cut. Twelfth run (local landing 3024,2360, 26fcc2a): two ingots and six raw iron held, two logs too, and thirteen minutes of tunnels at y 0 for coal until the trial timed out; held logs now burn before coal is mined for, and coal's stairs stop at y 40. Gym batch iron-a5 (26fcc2a): 0 of 5, but runs 1, 2 and 5 held flint and steel and a bucket and were cutting stairs up toward water when the trial's twenty minutes ran out; run 3 needed one more ingot and was :boxed; run 4 right-clicked its table three times to place a gravel, which opens a table, and failed :rejected; a block is now never placed on a table or furnace. Thirteenth run (local landing 2360,3000, 71bd06e): passed in 228 s, RCON finding a water bucket and flint and steel on the player; its staircase down was the one earlier runs had cut there. Gym batch iron-a6 run 1 (71bd06e): at the foot of its stairs between its table and furnace, no spot for the gravel to dig again for flint but the stair behind it, :no-spot three times; a block dug again at once may now go in a passage. Run 3: flint and steel and two ingots held, its tunnel at y 16 ran along an aquifer until water filled its floor, then stairs that could not be cut, :boxed three times; deeper stairs are now sent only where one can be cut, and with nothing to cut the bot gets out of the water and walks away to new rock. Runs 2 and 5 held flint and steel and the bucket and broke their pickaxes climbing out, with no table near and no wood left (:no-log, :no-path); the fill row now holds a spare pickaxe, made by the table before the climb, and one log is kept back from the furnace. Run 4 passed in 1043 s: 1 of 5. Fourteenth run (local landing 2360,2360, 58fc6aa): an ingot smelted at a furnace left by an earlier run, then flint wanted and no gravel in sight, so a tunnel at y 18 that ran over a hundred blocks east, over five gravel blocks in its own floor and past two iron ores in its wall; a block in the floor beside the feet now counts when digging it leaves a step down. Gym batch iron-a7 (58fc6aa): run 4 passed in 1028 s; run 1 held flint and steel and the bucket and climbed from y 16 to 44 under a lake, where sand and water over every stair refused it, stepped 32 east under the lake and failed :boxed, then wanted wood for a second pickaxe and failed :no-log; a climb's level steps now head for the nearest dry ground. Runs 2, 3 and 5 also ended :no-log: runs 2 and 3 held a working pickaxe and wanted wood for the second the fill row held, run 5 broke both on a long climb; the second pickaxe is now a spare, made only from what is held and near. Run 1 had crafted three tables on its way down, a log each; the bot now takes its table along when it goes out to gather or mine. Live run 15 (landing 3024,2360, 709ba16) passed in 435 s and run 16 (landing 2360,3000, 29bea58) in 704 s. Run 17 (landing 2360,2360, 0bc4550) found its gravel in the tunnel floor and carried its table, then climbed by stairs to the landing's height, which 145 blocks east was inside a hill, found no route to a pond 22 blocks off and waited :no-water; with nothing reachable and no open sky over it the bot now cuts stairs up until out of the ground. Gym batch iron-a8 (29bea58): 0 of 5. Runs 1 and 5 lost their table (run 1's walk back to it found no path; run 5 broke its pickaxe climbing with no table and no wood) and failed :no-log, which carrying the table addresses; run 4's stairs up ended inside a hill and it waited :no-water, which cutting out addresses; run 3's tunnel at y 16 was boxed and the stairs deeper it was sent down bordered water every way, :boxed twice in a second, so deeper stairs now need cells the dig will open; run 2 tunnelled 260 blocks east under the sea and its stairs up met the seabed, :boxed three times; tunnels now prefer headings with dry ground ahead, and a climb with no shore in sight steps toward the landing. Live run 18 (landing 2360,2360, 62c514a) passed in 408 s. Gym batch iron-a9 (62c514a) run 4's tunnel at y 2 met ore its stone pickaxe could not drop and failed :needs-tool three times; a level step now counts such a cell as refused and goes round it. Run 1 climbed out under the sea 155 blocks east of its landing and its level steps home were :boxed at 32 three times; a climb may now take as many more as the landing is far. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, afde46a): a bucket, one ingot and two stone pickaxes, standing at y 80, then three walks to ground at y 62, each a route that was accepted and then could not be walked, and the third ended the plan :no-path. A walk that fails :no-path now gives that place up and does not spend an attempt. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 5be14e7): three stone pickaxes worn out tunnelling for iron at y 16, one plank and a wooden pickaxe left, no log within 12 of the eye, and the plan waited :no-log until it failed. With no trunk in that band and the sky not open, the bot now walks to a remembered trunk a way leads to, else cuts stairs up. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 068485c): the same mine, the climb did start, six walks home failed :no-path within seconds and blacklisted the trunks, the wooden pickaxe broke on the stairs at y 32, and three :no-pickaxe failures ended the plan. :mine-iron now keeps a spare stone pickaxe and gathers the wood for it while one still digs; a gather that would wait :no-log is still no spare. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 29ef069): at spawn, before any tree was remembered, it cut a stair, failed :stair-not-taken, the walk to the one tree failed :no-path, and the plan waited :no-log. Stairs up for a log now wait until a trunk is remembered. Live run 19 (landing 3024,2360, 62c514a) printed RESULT :ok true holding a water bucket and flint and steel, but the judge read the 44 KB RESULT line half written and failed the trial on the reader's error; the gym now reads the bot's answer from its stdout pipe, a whole line at a time, and never polls the log. Run 3 dug gravel for flint at a ravine's edge at y -7, its collect walked after a drop and it fell from a high place, then timed out; a collect now stops at a ledge. Live run 20 (cbdcd23) lost its local server, frozen by the Mac's load (the watchdog killed it at a 60 s tick), and failed :no-answer. Run 5 hunted for water ten walks across mountains, then walked into a cocoa pod on a jungle log, which the hand list of awkward blocks lacked: three walks never moved it and failed :no-path; awkward blocks are now read from the game's collision shapes. Gym batch solid-b1 (6135175): run 9 stood on a hill at y 70 over ponds at y 62 and the rule that water more than five under the eye is cave water refused every one, :no-water; water under the open sky now counts however low. Run 6 broke its pickaxe on the stairs down in a stairwell one wide, where the only spot for a table was the stair and no niche could be cut without a pickaxe, :no-spot three times; a table, taken along when the bot goes on, may now stand in a passage. Run 1 climbed under the sea 146 blocks from its landing; its own tunnel home ran to the edge of the loaded chunks, the route came back :none and it cut stairs up under the sea until :boxed five times; a route that runs out of loaded terrain toward an unloaded target now counts as a way. Run 5 stood on a mountain at y 101 with 317 pools remembered, all refused by the depth rule (fixed above). Run 13 came up its stairs into a pit under the open sky, leaves and rock round it with no room to jump out; every pool near was cave water and no hunt had a route, :no-water; with no route anywhere the bot now tunnels out at its feet's height. Run 4 timed out tunnelling for its last three iron at y 2 for 25 minutes. Before that, steve: no race passed 3 ingots because the smelt burned planks as fuel and no bot mined coal; its two deepest runs (498, 518) reached two buckets and then hung at Fill Water Buckets in a dry jungle and a savanna. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 4528031): wood through a bucket and the portal kit, then from y 17 a new stair cut up through stone; the only stone pickaxe broke at y 49 and three :no-pickaxe failures ended the plan. The way down is already open, so a climb out walks to the sky before it cuts a stair. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 4e59246): flint and steel, a water bucket and the portal kit at the pond, then the pad's stand was stone inside the hill and three walks at it failed :no-path. The solid between the feet and a stand is dug. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, f277605): flint and steel, a water bucket and 283 cobblestone, then five hours walking out of the iron mine for a spare pickaxe and cutting back down. The mouth was under the sky and no trunk could be walked to, so the spare was never started. A walk up the dug shaft is not a spare; the mine continues. Race 38477665442 bot Clj_r20 (issue #36, the most frequent failure of the races: 99 real bots and 4,366 sim runs): six raw iron held, so the ingots wanted only fuel, and the coal row dug with any pickaxe and kept no spare; both stone pickaxes wore out in its tunnels at y 15, then it tunnelled on with the wooden one beside two sticks, a table and 249 cobblestone until that broke, :no-pickaxe. The fuel count had taken the two sticks as fuel, so the stone pickaxe they make was short of them. Sticks are now never fuel, and the coal row keeps a spare pickaxe made from what is carried. Race 38477665442 runner 8 (issue #37, the next most frequent: 29 real bots and 1,335 sim runs a round): five of its eight bots stopped :boxed at the ingots stood on the lip of a cave their staircase had broken into (Clj_r18 at y 87, 74 cobblestone held), every stair refused for the drop under it, and nothing else to cut from the lip, so the plan waited :boxed out. Each stair there had been taken by landing past the new cell's middle, perched on the edge of its floor with the feet in the next column, so the staircase was a shaft one block wide with no way back up. A stair's missing floor is now laid from carried cobblestone (a holder under the lip, then the floor), a stair ends only with the feet centred in its cell, and the walk onto a cell with nothing beyond it to stop the body creeps. Race 38477665442 (issue #40, 18 real bots): Clj_r21's stone pickaxe broke at y 60 in the iron mine; the stairs up stopped :no-pickaxe, the sticks for another were in the trees up top, and twelve walks to them failed :no-path. Fixed: a stair up is cut by hand when no pickaxe is held, 7500 ms a block (sim scenario stairs-up-with-no-pickaxe-are-cut-by-hand). Runner 9 (issue #66, and #59 at the cobblestone): Clj_r02 at y 57 dug the same sandstone cell three times, each FINISH queued by the lagging server behind another and dropped, the ack alone ending the dig; the stair walked into it and was put back ten times a second, :stair-not-taken three times. A dig now ends on the server's block update, its ack with the block standing is :rejected, and the staircase digs the cell again. Issue #72 (:no-shovel at the ingots, sim landing 2776,1816,108 in snow) is the stairs' tool rule, fixed with #42. Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, issue #67): bot Clj_r19 scooped its water, went back down for gravel and tunnelled at y 40 with its last two pickaxes until both broke, two sticks and 245 cobblestone in hand and the table left at the furnace; the gravel row now keeps a spare pickaxe as the coal row does, and the table is taken along before a scoop as before a mine. Same race, issue #39: bots Clj_r23 and Clj_r06 crafted the bucket at y 27 and 36 with one spare stone pickaxe and climbed out in one stairs-up of 26 and 53 stairs, more digs than the two pickaxes had, with no wood left for another (three logs taken from the forest, three pickaxes made); bot Clj_r22 tunnelled for coal at y 16 with a worn wooden pickaxe counted as its spare. Now a worn tool is no spare, a climb is cut in lengths the planner looks again between, and four sticks go down with the iron row's spare, gathered at the trees."
