 {:problem/stage :portal
  :problem/issue 8
  :problem/goals [:portal-kit :cast-one :portal :nether]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot must cast ten obsidian blocks from lava and water into a nether portal frame, light it and stand in it, which can only be done by following a fixed template mold, not by mining obsidian or improvising per cell."
  :problem/needs
  ["A site with no lava under the mold footprint (dx -2..6, dy -1..1, dz -2..3)"
   "Remembered lava sources within reach of the site, and water and lava as watched sightings"
   "The server's block-update for every place and pour, never a local prediction"
   "Which ops of the build plan are already satisfied, so a resume skips them"
   "The current dimension, from the respawn packet"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Lava pour lands on the bot's own feet (lidded cup or floor aim)"
   "Water aimed at the floor replaces the lava source instead of making obsidian"
   "Scooping late lets water spread and convert the lava pool"
   "Placing into a lava source destroys it; casting over a lava sea has no stance"
   "A rejected placement left as a ghost block; the pathfinder digs finished obsidian"
   "Lighting with the hitbox in the fire cell burns the bot"]
  :problem/done
  "Ten obsidian frame blocks and nether_portal blocks inside exist (RCON execute if block), and after standing in the portal RCON data get entity Dimension reads the Nether."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The mold is cast in the model from the kit to the Nether, resumed over six cells already cast and after a death; live cast-one passed 5/5 on the runners (batch p1-cast-one). The last failure, in the model: the site was chosen at the landing, so a death respawned the bot inside its own frame's corner and every walk out failed :no-path (vanilla never respawns a player inside blocks; a natural site near the world spawn still could put the frame over it). Before: ruststeve's blocker was casting over a lava sea and lidded cups bending pours onto the feet; steve went natural 0/63 versus arena 66/72, the wall being lava refill reachability. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 4e59246): at the pond with flint and steel, a water bucket and the portal kit, the pad's stand was stone inside the hill and three walks at it failed :no-path. The solid between the feet and a stand is dug. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, f277605): flint and steel, a water bucket and 283 cobblestone, then five hours walking out of the iron mine for a spare pickaxe and cutting back down. The mouth was under the sky and no trunk could be walked to. A walk up the dug shaft is not a spare; the mine continues, and the empty bucket the portal kit still needs can be smelted. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 61abf8c): flint and steel, a water bucket and 334 cobblestone at the pond, portal kit reached. The cast's first open pad cell was water and the stand for it was air over the next water cell; the walk there was :partial six times and three :no-path failures ended the plan. A place whose stand cannot be occupied is made from a cell that already reaches the block. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, ab3945e): a furnace and a stone pickaxe reached, then at y 32 every stair and every further level step was refused and three :stairs-down failures :boxed ended the plan. The cell a descent dies on is not stair'd again; the mine leaves it. Sim race 38395033917 (2026-10-13, world R3/24, 108 runs, issue #75): the portal kit wanted an empty bucket and 47 more cobblestone; the bot cut two staircases for stone, the second from the bottom of the first, and the second's first step dug out the first's riser, so no route led up (the :sky plan :none). Then, for the wood a new table needed, every walk to a trunk within the near band failed :no-path the tick it started and blacklisted that trunk, twelve a second, until the plan failed. A trunk in the band is now asked for a route before it is walked at, as the far ones were, so the bot climbs out instead (wood/near-walk). Open: a staircase cut from the bottom of another should not take the riser of the way back up. Race 38477665442 (issue #45, 18 real bots a round at cast-one): Clj_r25 scooped its water from a sand cell at a lake's edge under a bank two high; the pad's stand was over the water, the cell nearest it was the bank's top, which only cells over the water led to, and three builds failed :no-path walking at it while the sand cell itself reached the pad. Fixed: the stand chosen in the designated one's place is the nearest a route reaches (build-test a-stand-up-a-bank-is-passed-over-for-one-a-route-reaches). Clj_r06 built at y 16 in its iron mine with the only lava remembered sealed in rock fourteen blocks off: the refill's walk to that station has no route and tunnelling to it is not done yet. Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, issue #43): bot Clj_r04 held the kit and 488 cobblestone and wanted the empty bucket; its redig for flint had failed :not-picked-up at the cell before its feet, the table for a spare pickaxe went into that cell, and as a blacklisted position it did not count as near, so the bot went for the wood of a new table with its last pickaxe, found no route, climbed, and under a bed of gravel at y 42 stepped thirty cells along it, every stair refused, until the pickaxe broke. A place or a redig blacklists nothing now, and a climb steps out from under gravel before along it."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/08-portal-cast.md" "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-portal-mold.md" "brain/siblings/sib-steve-portal-cast.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-lava-safety.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :nether-and-fortress
  :problem/issue 11
  :problem/goals [:fortress]
  :problem/statement
  "The world value is overworld-only, so after a portal the bot cannot tell which dimension it is in, decodes Nether chunks with the wrong height, and has no safe way to reach a fortress across the lava sea."
  :problem/needs
  ["The dimension from login and respawn (sent as a registry index, 3 = the_nether)"
   "Per-dimension chunk height: Nether is min-y 0, 16 sections; overworld -64, 24 sections"
   "Sightings keyed by dimension, watching nether_bricks, spawner, portal, obsidian and lava"
   "Real chunk data after arrival before any step runs, not a timer"
   "Lava next to each tunnel step and missing floors ahead"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Chunks stay a snapshot of the dimension the bot is in, emptied on a change, as the server streams them again; memory keeps every dimension, each fact saying which"
   "A column's height is the sections the server sent (16 or 24), looked up in dimensions.edn: the reader thread decodes without knowing the dimension"
   "The dimension is the respawn's and login's name (:player/dimension, from #8), not the registry id, which only dimensions.edn's row order explains"
   "No lava capping: a cell behind a wall cannot be capped before the wall is dug, so a tunnel step never opens a cell beside lava and tries another step instead"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Stale overworld columns answer Nether lookups (a brick reported exactly 64 blocks off)"
   "Parsing a Nether chunk as 24 sections runs off the buffer"
   "Overworld goals (mine iron) run in the Nether"
   "Falling into the lava sea on an open approach to the fortress"
   "Fortress brick picked below the lava sea surface"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON confirms the bot is in minecraft:the_nether with nether_bricks under its feet or within 6 blocks, RESULT :ok true, and zero deaths counted."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never attempted this. ruststeve: after entering the Nether its overworld columns answered Nether lookups (fortress brick reported 64 blocks too low) and the parser panicked on the shorter Nether chunk; finding the fortress was solved, but reaching it alive was not, with 9+ falls into the lava sea at one spot."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/09-nether-and-fortress.md" "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dimension-change.md"]}
